The writer skill (.claude/skills/writer) adapts jtydhr88/screenwriting-skills (MIT, sw-dialogue) and
coreyhaines31/marketingskills (MIT, copywriting, ai-tells, ad-creative hook system). Shot-design rules in the
director skill also draw on zenstory-ai/drama-skills (MIT).

The director skill (.claude/skills/director) (five anchors, scene formula, three-jobs and three-detail rules,
one motivated camera move, rhythm ladder, Murch's rule of six) adapts smixs/visual-skills by Serge Shima (https://github.com/smixs/visual-skills),
licensed CC BY 4.0 (https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/). Changes: translated to Korean, condensed,
and mapped onto Fluma's storyboard fields and lint checks.


The humanizer-ko skill (.claude/skills/humanizer-ko) is DaleSeo/korean-skills `humanizer` (MIT, Copyright (c) 2026 Dale Seo,
https://github.com/daleseo/korean-skills, commit ae12ba2), renamed only; its license is in that folder. The writer skill
summarizes its Korean AI-style patterns (KatFishNet, arXiv 2503.00032).

